>   - Each patch is a four-sided band between two lines. Boundaries sit on the character lines and near inflection zones, never in the middle of a highlight. (25 October 2026, 21:48:21 +0100)
>   - A crisp line is a G0 boundary (position only, so the edge stays sharp). Areas that should read smooth are either one surface, or a G1/G2 match plus a small fillet. (25 October 2026, 21:48:21 +0100)
>   - Curves are faired before any surface exists, and quality is judged with reflection lines (zebra), not wireframe. (25 October 2026, 21:48:21 +0100)
